---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="How Tenure Works | Memory and Agent Enforcement"
  description="See how Tenure gives every AI request the right memory, limits the tools an agent can use, and verifies required evidence before an action runs."
>
  <main class="how-it-works-page">
    <section id="how-hero" class="hiw-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="label">How it works</span>
        <h1>Control what AI knows and <br /> what agents can do.</h1>
        <p class="section-lede">
          Tenure sits between your application and the model. It adds the right memory, removes tools the agent should not use, and checks every returned action before it reaches your systems.
        </p>
        <p class="hero-point">
          Memory shapes the decision. Policy decides whether that decision can become an action.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="request-path" class="section-surface hiw-section">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="label">One request path</span>
        <h2>Context goes in. Governed actions come out.</h2>
        <p class="section-lede">
          One authenticated token tells Tenure which memory the caller may receive and which agent policy it must enforce.
        </p>

        <div class="request-flow" aria-label="Tenure request path">
          <article class="flow-card">
            <span>01</span>
            <strong>Identify</strong>
            <small>Resolve the caller, memory scope, and agent policy.</small>
          </article>
          <div class="flow-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <article class="flow-card memory-card">
            <span>02</span>
            <strong>Inject memory</strong>
            <small>Inject approved context relevant to this request.</small>
          </article>
          <div class="flow-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <article class="flow-card">
            <span>03</span>
            <strong>Filter tools</strong>
            <small>Hide capabilities outside the active policy.</small>
          </article>
          <div class="flow-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <article class="flow-card model-card">
            <span>04</span>
            <strong>Call the model</strong>
            <small>Send the governed request to the provider.</small>
          </article>
          <div class="flow-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <article class="flow-card">
            <span>05</span>
            <strong>Check evidence</strong>
            <small>Verify the action, arguments, and preconditions.</small>
          </article>
          <div class="flow-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <article class="flow-card decision-card">
            <span>06</span>
            <strong>Release or block</strong>
            <small>Return safe actions and withhold everything else.</small>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="principle-grid">
          <article>
            <span class="card-label">Memory</span>
            <h3>What should the model know?</h3>
            <p>Only active, relevant context from data scopes this token is allowed to access.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="card-label">Policy</span>
            <h3>What may the agent do?</h3>
            <p>Only reviewed tools, arguments, and output attached to its identity.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="card-label">Preconditions</span>
            <h3>What must be true first?</h3>
            <p>Required evidence from earlier steps must exist before a dependent action continues.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="memory" class="hiw-section">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="label">How memory works</span>
        <h2>Tenure turns useful context into governed memory.</h2>
        <p class="section-lede">
          Conversations, documentation, code context, and direct input can become structured beliefs. Each belief keeps its source and scope, so Tenure can decide when it belongs in a request.
        </p>

        <div class="four-grid">
          <article class="step-card">
            <span class="step-number">01</span>
            <h3>Capture</h3>
            <p>Learn decisions, facts, preferences, constraints, and open questions from the sources you choose.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="step-card">
            <span class="step-number">02</span>
            <h3>Structure</h3>
            <p>Store a compact belief with type, source, scope, confidence, and history instead of a transcript dump.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="step-card">
            <span class="step-number">03</span>
            <h3>Govern</h3>
            <p>Review, edit, approve, reinforce, supersede, or keep a belief out of model context.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="step-card featured-step">
            <span class="step-number">04</span>
            <h3>Inject</h3>
            <p>Supply only active memory allowed for this caller and relevant to the current turn.</p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="scope-example">
          <div class="scope-stack">
            <div class="scope-row active-scope"><span>ORG</span><strong>Never send customer secrets to third party tools.</strong></div>
            <div class="scope-row active-scope"><span>TEAM</span><strong>Platform APIs use structured error envelopes.</strong></div>
            <div class="scope-row active-scope"><span>PROJECT</span><strong>Payments migration targets PostgreSQL 18.</strong></div>
            <div class="scope-row inactive-scope"><span>USER</span><strong>Prefer detailed explanations with examples.</strong></div>
          </div>
          <div class="scope-result">
            <span class="card-label">agent:code-reviewer</span>
            <h3>Three beliefs are eligible.</h3>
            <p>Organization, team, and project memory can enter the request. User persona memory stays out because this token cannot access it.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="detail-links">
          <a href="/how-it-works/belief-extraction">Belief extraction &rarr;</a>
          <a href="/how-it-works/belief-merging">Belief merging &rarr;</a>
          <a href="/how-it-works/contradiction-handling">Contradiction handling &rarr;</a>
          <a href="/how-it-works/knowledge-sources">Knowledge sources &rarr;</a>
        </div>

        <p class="boundary-note">
          Memory helps the model reason with the right context. It does not grant authority. Agent policy separately decides what the model may do.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="enforcement" class="section-surface hiw-section" style="background: var(--surface);">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="label">How enforcement works</span>
        <h2>Tenure controls both sides of the model call.</h2>
        <p class="section-lede">
          Before the model runs, Tenure adds approved memory and removes forbidden tools. After the model responds, Tenure checks every structured action again.
        </p>

        <div class="enforcement-flow">
          <div class="enforcement-column">
            <span class="column-title">Application supplies</span>
            <div class="tool-row keep"><code>fetch_customer</code><b>KEEP</b></div>
            <div class="tool-row keep"><code>generate_email</code><b>KEEP</b></div>
            <div class="tool-row remove"><code>delete_customer</code><b>REMOVE</b></div>
            <div class="tool-row remove"><code>export_database</code><b>REMOVE</b></div>
          </div>
          <div class="enforcement-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <div class="enforcement-column highlighted-column">
            <span class="column-title">Model sees</span>
            <div class="tool-row keep"><code>fetch_customer</code><b>VISIBLE</b></div>
            <div class="tool-row keep"><code>generate_email</code><b>VISIBLE</b></div>
          </div>
          <div class="enforcement-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <div class="enforcement-column">
            <span class="column-title">Tenure decides</span>
            <div class="tool-row release"><code>generate_email</code><b>CHECK</b></div>
            <div class="tool-row block"><code>delete_customer</code><b>BLOCK</b></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="four-grid">
          <article class="plain-card">
            <h3>Add approved context</h3>
            <p>Only memory that is relevant, active, and allowed for the token enters the request.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="plain-card">
            <h3>Hide forbidden tools</h3>
            <p>Capabilities outside policy are removed before inference. The model never sees them.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="plain-card">
            <h3>Check returned actions</h3>
            <p>Tools, arguments, and required evidence are verified before release to your runtime.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="plain-card">
            <h3>Check standalone actions</h3>
            <p>Calls with no ancestor and no evidence chain are still checked against policy, not waved through by default.</p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <p class="boundary-note">
          When an action is blocked, your team chooses what happens next. Tenure can return a hard error, or hand the rejection to your own application logic for retry, fallback, or rerouting to a different agent.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="preconditions" class="hiw-section">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="label">Required evidence</span>
        <h2>Allowed does not always mean allowed yet.</h2>
        <p class="section-lede">
          A policy can require an earlier tool call to return specific evidence before the next action is released. Tenure calls these requirements preconditions. Each check verifies three things: that the field is present, that its type matches what was observed, and that its value satisfies the rule your team approved.
        </p>

        <div class="precondition-flow">
          <article class="precondition-card">
            <span class="step-number">01</span>
            <h3>Fetch the customer</h3>
            <code>fetch_customer</code>
            <p>The agent calls the required capability first.</p>
          </article>
          <div class="flow-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <article class="precondition-card evidence-card">
            <span class="step-number">02</span>
            <h3>Verify the result</h3>
            <div class="evidence-row">
              <div class="evidence-row-head"><code>customer_id</code><b>MATCH</b></div>
              <small class="evidence-meta">String &middot; matches customer_id sent to generate_email</small>
            </div>
            <div class="evidence-row">
              <div class="evidence-row-head"><code>active</code><b>EQUALS</b></div>
              <small class="evidence-meta">Boolean &middot; must equal true</small>
            </div>
            <div class="evidence-row">
              <div class="evidence-row-head"><code>tier</code><b>VALID</b></div>
              <small class="evidence-meta">String &middot; non-empty, any observed value</small>
            </div>
          </article>
          <div class="flow-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <article class="precondition-card release-card">
            <span class="step-number">03</span>
            <h3>Release the next action</h3>
            <code>generate_email</code>
            <p>The action continues only when every enabled check passes.</p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="outcome-grid">
          <article class="outcome-card pass-outcome">
            <span>RELEASED</span>
            <h3>Required evidence exists</h3>
            <p>The dependent action can continue to your runtime.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="outcome-card fail-outcome">
            <span>BLOCKED</span>
            <h3>Required evidence is missing</h3>
            <p>Tenure withholds the action before it reaches your runtime.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="outcome-card config-outcome">
            <span>CONFIGURABLE</span>
            <h3>Your team chooses the checks</h3>
            <p>Proposed preconditions can be turned on or off in the draft policy.</p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <p class="boundary-note">
          Most tools ask whether an action is allowed. Tenure also asks whether the agent has established everything required to perform it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    

    <section id="policy-lifecycle" class="section-surface hiw-section">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="label">From observation to enforcement</span>
        <h2>Start with what the agent actually does.</h2>
        <p class="section-lede">
          Tenure records the tools an agent sees, the calls it makes, and the results returned between steps. It turns that behavior into a draft policy your team can review.
        </p>

        <div class="policy-flow">
          <article><span>01</span><strong>Observe</strong><small>Record tools, calls, inputs, and results, and track which available tools were never invoked.</small></article>
          <div>&rarr;</div>
          <article><span>02</span><strong>Draft</strong><small>Propose capabilities and preconditions.</small></article>
          <div>&rarr;</div>
          <article><span>03</span><strong>Review</strong><small>Choose what is allowed and required.</small></article>
          <div>&rarr;</div>
          <article><span>04</span><strong>Publish</strong><small>Attach the policy to an agent token.</small></article>
          <div>&rarr;</div>
          <article class="policy-final"><span>05</span><strong>Enforce</strong><small>Apply it to every request.</small></article>
        </div>

        <div class="three-grid">
          <article class="plain-card">
            <span class="card-label">Observed exposure</span>
            <h3>What could the agent use?</h3>
            <p>See every tool the application made available to the model, and which of those capabilities were never invoked during observation.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="plain-card">
            <span class="card-label">Observed use</span>
            <h3>What did the agent do?</h3>
            <p>See calls, arguments, outputs, and evidence passed between steps.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="plain-card featured-plain">
            <span class="card-label">Reviewed policy</span>
            <h3>What should remain possible?</h3>
            <p>Choose allowed capabilities and enable or disable proposed preconditions.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="hiw-section">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="label">Built to be inspected</span>
        <h2>See what the model knew and why an action was allowed.</h2>
        <p class="section-lede">
          Tenure records memory and enforcement as the request happens. You do not have to reconstruct the decision after something goes wrong.
        </p>

        <div class="record-grid">
          <article class="record-card">
            <span class="card-label">Memory record</span>
            <h3>What entered the request?</h3>
            <p>See which beliefs were injected, their source and scope, and why they were eligible.</p>
            <strong>What did the model know?</strong>
          </article>
          <article class="record-card">
            <span class="card-label">Observation record</span>
            <h3>What did the agent attempt?</h3>
            <p>See available tools, invoked tools, arguments, outputs, and evidence paths, and drill into the exact observation behind any summarized frequency.</p>
            <strong>What did the agent try to do?</strong>
          </article>
          <article class="record-card featured-record">
            <span class="card-label">Enforcement record</span>
            <h3>Why was it released or blocked?</h3>
            <p>See identity, policy version, capability decision, precondition result, and outcome.</p>
            <strong>Why did Tenure make this decision?</strong>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="protocol-boundary" class="section-surface hiw-section">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="label">Works across agents and models</span>
        <h2>Change the framework without rewriting the rules.</h2>
        <p class="section-lede">
          Tenure runs on the model request path instead of inside one agent framework. The same memory scopes, tool policy, preconditions, and audit rules apply instantly to any traffic using standard OpenAI and Anthropic protocols.
        </p>

        <div class="protocol-flow">
          <div class="protocol-stack">
            <span>Custom agent</span>
            <span>Agent framework</span>
            <span>Application code</span>
            <span>AI client</span>
          </div>
          <div class="protocol-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <div class="protocol-box">
            <span class="card-label">Supported ingress</span>
            <strong>OpenAI and Anthropic protocols</strong>
            <small>Normalize requests and returned actions.</small>
          </div>
          <div class="protocol-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <div class="protocol-box tenure-box">
            <span class="card-label">Tenure</span>
            <strong>Memory and policy gateway</strong>
            <small>Resolve context, filter tools, verify evidence, and record decisions.</small>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="recap" class="hiw-section">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="label">The full picture</span>
        <h2>One request path answers six questions.</h2>

        <div class="recap-grid">
          <div><span>Who is making this request?</span><strong>Token identity</strong></div>
          <div><span>What should the model know?</span><strong>Scoped memory</strong></div>
          <div><span>Which tools should it see?</span><strong>Capability policy</strong></div>
          <div><span>What did the agent try to do?</span><strong>Observation</strong></div>
          <div><span>Has the required evidence been established?</span><strong>Preconditions</strong></div>
          <div><span>Why was the action released or blocked?</span><strong>Enforcement audit</strong></div>
        </div>

        <p class="boundary-note">
          Memory gives the model the right context. Policy limits its authority. Preconditions verify what must be true before that authority can be used.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="cta" class="section-surface hiw-section">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="label">Get started</span>
        <h2>Put memory and enforcement on the same request path.</h2>
        <p class="cta-sub">
          Give every AI request the right context, observe what agents actually do, and enforce reviewed policy before actions reach your systems.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-cta-row">
          <a href="/pricing" class="btn-primary">View Pricing</a>
          <a href="/docs/quickstart" class="btn-secondary">Get Started</a>
        </div>
        <p class="cta-meta">Self-hosted <span>&middot;</span> No call-home telemetry</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <style>
    .how-it-works-page *,
    .how-it-works-page *::before,
    .how-it-works-page *::after {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    .hiw-hero {
      padding: 7rem 0 5rem;
      text-align: center;
      align-content: center;
    }

    .hiw-hero h1 {
      max-width: 1100px;
    }


    .hero-point {
      max-width: 1100px;
      margin-top: 1.5rem;
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    .hiw-section {
      padding: 5rem 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }


    .request-flow {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr;
      gap: 0.65rem;
      align-items: stretch;
      margin-top: 2.5rem;
    }

    .flow-card,
    .step-card,
    .plain-card,
    .precondition-card,
    .outcome-card,
    .record-card,
    .protocol-box,
    .principle-grid article {
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 14px;
      background: var(--surface2);
    }

    .flow-card {
      min-width: 0;
      padding: 1rem;
    }

    .flow-card span,
    .step-number,
    .policy-flow article span {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
      color: var(--accent);
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.68rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    }

    .flow-card strong,
    .flow-card small,
    .policy-flow strong,
    .policy-flow small,
    .protocol-box strong,
    .protocol-box small {
      display: block;
    }

    .flow-card strong {
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
    }

    .flow-card small {
      margin-top: 0.45rem;
      color: var(--dim);
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      line-height: 1.45;
    }

    .flow-arrow,
    .enforcement-arrow,
    .protocol-arrow {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      color: var(--dim);
    }

    .memory-card,
    .decision-card,
    .featured-step,
    .release-card,
    .featured-plain,
    .featured-record,
    .tenure-box {
      border-color: rgba(0, 168, 173, 0.38);
      background: rgba(0, 168, 173, 0.055);
    }

    .model-card {
      border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.16);
    }

    .principle-grid,
    .three-grid,
    .outcome-grid,
    .record-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1rem;
      margin-top: 1.5rem;
    }

    .principle-grid article,
    .plain-card,
    .outcome-card,
    .record-card {
      padding: 1.35rem;
    }

    .card-label,
    .column-title,
    .outcome-card > span {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
      color: var(--accent);
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.68rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .principle-grid h3,
    .plain-card h3,
    .outcome-card h3,
    .record-card h3,
    .step-card h3,
    .precondition-card h3 {
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .principle-grid p,
    .plain-card p,
    .outcome-card p,
    .record-card p,
    .step-card p,
    .precondition-card p {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 0.86rem;
    }

    .four-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1rem;
      margin-top: 2.5rem;
    }

    .step-card {
      padding: 1.35rem;
    }

    .scope-example {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
      margin-top: 1rem;
    }

    .scope-stack,
    .scope-result {
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 14px;
      background: var(--surface2);
      padding: 1rem;
    }

    .scope-stack {
      display: grid;
      gap: 0.65rem;
    }

    .scope-row {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 80px 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
      align-items: center;
      padding: 0.75rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 9px;
    }

    .scope-row span {
      color: var(--accent);
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.66rem;
    }

    .scope-row strong {
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: 0.82rem;
    }

    .inactive-scope {
      opacity: 0.42;
    }

    .scope-result {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      justify-content: center;
      border-color: rgba(0, 168, 173, 0.3);
    }

    .scope-result h3 {
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .detail-links {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 0.75rem;
      margin-top: 1.25rem;
    }

    .detail-links a {
      padding: 0.55rem 0.8rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 8px;
      background: var(--surface2);
      color: var(--muted);
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.72rem;
    }

    .detail-links a:hover {
      border-color: var(--accent);
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .boundary-note {
      margin: 2rem 0 0;
      padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;
      border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
      background: rgba(0, 168, 173, 0.045);
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: 0.92rem;
    }

    .enforcement-flow {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
      margin-top: 2.5rem;
      align-items: stretch;
    }

    .enforcement-column {
      padding: 1.1rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 14px;
      background: var(--surface2);
    }

    .highlighted-column {
      border-color: rgba(0, 168, 173, 0.3);
    }

    .tool-row {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 0.75rem;
      padding: 0.65rem 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    .tool-row:last-child {
      border-bottom: 0;
    }

    .tool-row code {
      color: var(--text);
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.75rem;
    }

    .tool-row b {
      color: var(--accent);
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.65rem;
    }

    .tool-row.remove,
    .tool-row.hidden {
      opacity: 0.42;
    }

    .tool-row.block b {
      color: var(--red);
    }

    .precondition-flow {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
      align-items: stretch;
      margin-top: 2.5rem;
    }

    .precondition-card {
      padding: 1.4rem;
    }

    .precondition-card > code {
      display: inline-block;
